 R←Test_004(debugFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;⎕WSID;ns;assets;before;new;lines;question;file
⍝ Exercise what `Notify` hands over to `toast.ps1`: a title that identifies the session, the
⍝ question as the body, and the icon.
⍝ The assets folder used here holds no `toast.ps1`, so nothing pops up and, because nobody
⍝ reads it, the file `Notify` wrote is still there to be inspected.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '∘∘∘ ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 :If 'Win'≢3↑⊃# ⎕WG'APLVersion'
     R←T._WindowsOnly ⋄ →0
 :EndIf

 new←⍬
 assets←2 ⎕NQ'.' 'GetEnvironment' 'TEMP'
 ns←⎕NS''
 {}ns.⎕FX ##.WindowsToast.⎕NR'Notify'
 {}'TatinVars'ns.⎕NS''
 {}ns.TatinVars.⎕FX(' r←GetFullPath2AssetsFolder')(' r←''',assets,'''')

 question←'Test_004: delete /var/log/app.log?'
 ⎕WSID←'Test_004_WS'                            ⍝ Localised in the header, so leaving undoes it
 before←⊃0 1 ⎕NINFO⍠1⊢assets,'/dyalog-notify-*.txt'
 {}ns.Notify'YesOrNo'question
 new←(⊃0 1 ⎕NINFO⍠1⊢assets,'/dyalog-notify-*.txt')~before
 →T.GoToTidyUp 1≠≢new
 lines←⊃⎕NGET(⊃new)1
 →T.GoToTidyUp 3≠≢lines

 →T.GoToTidyUp'Test_004_WS'≢⊃lines              ⍝ The workspace name identifies the session
 →T.GoToTidyUp question≢2⊃lines
 :If 0<≢3⊃lines                                 ⍝ The icon is empty when DYALOG is not set
     →T.GoToTidyUp'dyalog.exe'≢¯10↑3⊃lines
 :EndIf

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 :For file :In new                          ⍝ `⎕NDELETE` is shy, so no `{}` here
     ⎕NDELETE file
 :EndFor
⍝Done
